  "version": 1,
  "matching": [
    "1. Avoid overly broad keywords that commonly appear in unrelated sentences.",
    "2. Prefer specific phrases over single generic words.",
    "3. When a keyword has known false positives, use phrase exclusions (exclude) or mark it as weak (weakKeywords).",
    "4. If multiple categories match, choose the strongest match, not just list order.",
    "5. general is the fallback when no sufficiently relevant category is detected.",
    "Scoring: each keyword hit = 2 points, each weakKeywords hit = 1 point. Matching ignores upper/lower case; English keywords match whole words only.",
    "exclude: phrases removed from the input before this category is scored (e.g. 'due date' for date).",
    "yieldsTo: if any listed category also scores, this category steps aside (e.g. health yields to work).",
    "Highest score wins. Tie: the category whose matched keywords are longer (more specific) wins. Still tied: listed first wins. Zero points: general."
